CORE gcc-only
priority.c

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[a_101\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ assertion n == 5: SUCCESS$
^\[a_101\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ assertion order\[i\] == i \+ 1: SUCCESS$
^\[a_101\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ assertion 0: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ assertion n == 0: SUCCESS$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Destructors with a priority run in descending priority order, the exact reverse
of constructors; the failing assertion shows that the last destructor runs.
